{"type":"standard","title":"Thai Song language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Thai Song language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q7709159","titles":{"canonical":"Thai_Song_language","normalized":"Thai Song language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Thai Song language</span></span>"},"pageid":35199605,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Tai_dam_language.jpg/330px-Tai_dam_language.jpg","width":330,"height":406},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Tai_dam_language.jpg","width":1040,"height":1280},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1330693495","tid":"848d85d8-e767-11f0-8143-540641efa391","timestamp":"2026-01-01T23:13:44Z","description":"Tai language of Thailand","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thai_Song_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thai_Song_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thai_Song_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Thai_Song_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thai_Song_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Thai_Song_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thai_Song_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Thai_Song_language"}},"extract":"Thai Song, or Lao Song, is a Tai language of Thailand. The Tai Song originally settled in Phetchaburi Province, and from there went to settle in various provinces such as Kanchanaburi, Ratchaburi, Suphanburi, Nakhon Pathom, Samut Sakhon, Samut Songkhram, Nakhon Sawan, and Phitsanulok.","extract_html":"<p><b>Thai Song</b>, or <b>Lao Song</b>, is a Tai language of Thailand. The Tai Song originally settled in Phetchaburi Province, and from there went to settle in various provinces such as Kanchanaburi, Ratchaburi, Suphanburi, Nakhon Pathom, Samut Sakhon, Samut Songkhram, Nakhon Sawan, and Phitsanulok.</p>"}